# Accessibility

## Motion

- Honor `prefers-reduced-motion: reduce` — disable parallax, smooth scroll overrides, and entrance animations.
- Provide skip buttons for timed overlays (see `intro-skip.tsx`).
- Do not rely on motion alone to convey information.

## Semantic HTML

- Use correct heading hierarchy (`h1` once per page).
- Interactive elements must be `<button>` or `<a>`, not `<div onClick>`.
- Images require meaningful `alt` text — enforce in CMS schema validation where possible.

## Focus and keyboard

- All interactive controls must be keyboard reachable.
- Visible focus styles — do not remove outlines without a replacement.
- Skip links for main content when navigation is complex.

## Color and contrast

- Use semantic tokens from `src/styles/tokens/semantic.css` — they support light/dark.
- Do not convey state by color alone; pair with text or icons.

## Lab pages

`/lab/*` routes are `noindex` — fine for internal reference, but still follow a11y for dev testing.
